    "created_at": "2020-02-25T20:57:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-25T20:57:21Z",
    "body": "Serverside/backend validation and checking is always necessary, as requests can also originate from outside of the browser (e.g. curl). This proposal/request isn't meant to replace serverside validation _(which it can't)_ but only to try and prevent the user from doing wrong things _(which they do)_.\r\n\r\nI like to compare it with `input type=\"email\"` and the like: this input type pushes the user in a certain direction and prevents them from entering wrong input (or at least warns them about it). This however doesn't mean a developer can therefore omit the verification part on the backend, as user-input can never be trusted.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
