    "created_at": "2025-04-18T19:55:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-18T19:55:47Z",
    "body": "I'm hesitant to change the default behavior due to compat risk. I tried to fix a double submit related bug in chromium once, and it resulted in many regressions which I wrote WPTs for. See the list of issues in the bug description here: https://issues.chromium.org/issues/40136560\n\nForm submission already uses an asynchronous task which prevents double submission in the case where the main thread does multiple submissions, such as calling form.submit() in the click event handler of a submit button. I'm not sure if this is specced, but the WPTs and compat we have explains this decently well.\n\nIf we have an opt-in to do this, what should the mechanism be?\n- Disable the form element\n- Disable the submit button\n- Mark an internal flag on the form element, and don't fire the submit event\n- Mark an internal flag on the form element, fire the submit event, but don't do anything with it\n\nWhat conditions should re-enable form submission afterwards?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
