    "body": "From today's WHATNOT:\n\n> Simon: in last comment linked, I porosed using a formal validation mechanism as the way to solve this problem.  Just checking if there’s interest/concern from others.\nJoey: your suggestion should not break websites.  Hopefully nothing should break with that.\nMason: is there a time limit?  If I submit and come back an hour later and submit, does it error again?\nSimon: maybe a five second limit or something?\nMason: just calling out the difference between accidental double-submit and intentional second submit.\nSimon: soln to users wanting to submit again is they get a validation message and they can click again to do the submission.\nMason: so the validation message says “click here to submit again?”\nSimon: yes.\nLuke: I’m not against the issue but I’m not sure it’s a big enough issue to fix as a web platform fix; you’re probably handling on the server?  Doesn’t warrant too much complexity to fix, at least.\nMason: only counterpoint to that is when Joey solved some of this a while back there are definitely a prevalence of sites that do nothing to fix this.  PRobably long tail sites, but still.\nPanos: sounds like a plausible solution, you’re going to create a spec PR?\nSimon: yes\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
